# Security Skills (2025–2026)

## How to Use This File

This file catalogs 20 foundational-to-advanced skills specific to application security within the Laravel ecosystem. Each skill includes a concise definition, a real-world usage trigger, and a source reference.

When assisting users, match their request to the most relevant skill name and cite it when explaining recommendations. Prioritize defensive patterns and framework-provided protections before suggesting third-party security tools.

Apply Laravel 13 security defaults for new applications; when auditing legacy systems, document existing gaps and provide incremental hardening paths that align with current framework versions.

Source URLs point to official Laravel documentation and OWASP references. For patterns without dedicated Laravel docs (e.g., secrets management, security headers), the best available reference is used.

## Skill Catalog

- **OWASP Top 10 Mitigation in Laravel** — applies framework features to prevent injection, XSS, broken auth, and other critical risks. *Use when:* conducting security reviews, hardening new features, or preparing for penetration tests. *Source:* https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten
- **CSRF Protection (Web vs API)** — enforces token validation for state-changing web requests while keeping stateless APIs stateless. *Use when:* building form-based apps, securing SPA integrations, or configuring Sanctum authentication. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/csrf
- **XSS Prevention via Blade Escaping** — auto-escapes output in templates and restricts raw HTML rendering to trusted content. *Use when:* rendering user-generated content, integrating rich text editors, or preventing script injection. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/blade#displaying-data
- **SQL Injection Prevention via Parameter Binding** — uses query builders or Eloquent to safely interpolate values without string concatenation. *Use when:* building dynamic queries, accepting user filters, or constructing report generators. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/queries
- **Mass Assignment Protection ($fillable/$guarded)** — whitelists attributes eligible for bulk assignment from untrusted HTTP request payloads. *Use when:* accepting user input for model creation, preventing privilege escalation, or enforcing integrity. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/eloquent#mass-assignment
- **Authorization via Gates & Policies** — defines ability checks and model-specific rules for fine-grained access control implementation. *Use when:* implementing role-based permissions, restricting resource access, or auditing authorization decisions. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/authorization
- **Encryption at Rest for Sensitive Data** — encrypts database columns or files using Laravel's built-in cryptographic facilities securely. *Use when:* storing PII, complying with GDPR/HIPAA, or protecting API keys in configuration. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/encryption
- **bcrypt & Argon2 Hashing Strategies** — uses adaptive, salted hashing for passwords with configurable computational cost factors. *Use when:* implementing user authentication, migrating legacy hashes, or meeting password policies. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/hashing
- **Auth Session Management** — configures secure session cookie flags, idle/absolute timeouts, and multi-device logout to limit stolen-session blast radius. *Use when:* hardening high-value accounts, enforcing compliance session policies, or invalidating sessions after credential changes. *Source:* training
- **Multi-Factor Auth (MFA)** — adds a second factor via TOTP authenticator apps or WebAuthn passkeys on top of password authentication. *Use when:* protecting admin panels, meeting regulatory MFA requirements, or reducing account takeover risk from credential leaks. *Source:* training
- **Signed URLs for Temporary Access** — generates time-limited, tamper-proof URLs for password resets or secure file downloads. *Use when:* enabling secure email links, providing expiring resources, or preventing URL guessing. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/urls#signed-urls
- **Rate Limiting as Security Control** — throttles authentication attempts and API calls to prevent brute force and enumeration. *Use when:* protecting login endpoints, mitigating automated attacks, or enforcing fair usage policies. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/routing#rate-limiting
- **Secrets Management with Vault/AWS** — stores credentials in dedicated secret management stores instead of plain environment variables. *Use when:* managing production credentials, enabling automated rotation, or complying with security policies. *Source:* training
- **Dependency CVE Scanning (Roave)** — checks Composer dependencies for known vulnerabilities automatically during continuous integration builds. *Use when:* preventing supply chain attacks, maintaining compliance, or justifying dependency updates. *Source:* training
- **HTTPS Enforcement & HSTS Headers** — redirects HTTP traffic to HTTPS and configures Strict-Transport-Security to prevent downgrades. *Use when:* securing production deployments, meeting browser requirements, or enabling HTTP/2 protocols. *Source:* training
- **Security Headers Configuration** — sets Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options, and Referrer-Policy via application middleware layers. *Use when:* mitigating clickjacking, preventing XSS payloads, or reducing information leakage vectors. *Source:* training
- **CORS Configuration for Cross-Origin APIs** — defines allowed origins, methods, and headers for safe browser-based cross-origin consumption. *Use when:* building public APIs, supporting frontend frameworks, or enabling third-party integrations. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/cors
- **Sensitive Data Logging Redaction** — masks passwords, tokens, and PII in application logs to prevent accidental credential exposure. *Use when:* debugging production issues, complying with privacy regulations, or enabling safe log aggregation. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/logging
- **Request Forgery Protection Enhancements (Laravel 13+)** — adds origin-aware verification via PreventRequestForgery middleware for advanced CSRF defense. *Use when:* hardening against modern CSRF attacks, supporting browser security standards, or meeting enterprise audits. *Source:* training
- **Attribute-Based Authorization (Laravel 13+)** — uses #[Authorize] attribute for declarative policy checks directly on controller methods. *Use when:* simplifying authorization logic, enabling route-level permissions, or improving code readability. *Source:* training

